{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AX2dYM6bx6XbYb5wFnsbCM","type":"tool_result","content":"95:## 9. Self-checks that cry wolf are still worth keeping\n102:## 10. Process traps in the harness itself\n116:## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n125:## 12. The engine stops reproducing itself part-way through a long run, so \"bit-identical token ids\" is not a test there\n179:## 13. A gate that passed, reported as a failure, because the probe it rode on kept no records\n200:## 14. A phase that ran nothing, and reported \"finished\"\n239:## 15. Put a leg the change *cannot* touch inside the same sweep\n278:## 16. A fitted slope is only \"cost per 1000 context\" if the mark is linear in context\n313:## 17. A launch that failed, and a `cudaStreamSynchronize` that called it success\n393:## 18. The device opt-in maximum is not the kernel's maximum, and the safety margin that failed a passing gate\n428:## 19. The variance is BETWEEN checkpoint loads, not within them — 0.6 % vs 5.7 %\n471:## 20. A gate that does not compile is a gate that passes by never running (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n519:## 21. dprof reads a saving 15–20 % low, so it attributes but does not ratchet (ladder 1.5)\n542:## 22. `tau` reproduced to four decimals; `tok/s` on the same protocol did not — and the promotion gate keys on the second one (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd851466-8fe9-421b-9d36-f2763d695418","uuid":"c6b8cbde-3d83-4545-8f59-ebc82b6d9c4e","timestamp":"2026-08-20T15:17:04.037Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"95:## 9. Self-checks that cry wolf are still worth keeping\n102:## 10. Process traps in the harness itself\n116:## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n125:## 12. The engine stops reproducing itself part-way through a long run, so \"bit-identical token ids\" is not a test there\n179:## 13. A gate that passed, reported as a failure, because the probe it rode on kept no records\n200:## 14. A phase that ran nothing, and reported \"finished\"\n239:## 15. Put a leg the change *cannot* touch inside the same sweep\n278:## 16. A fitted slope is only \"cost per 1000 context\" if the mark is linear in context\n313:## 17. A launch that failed, and a `cudaStreamSynchronize` that called it success\n393:## 18. The device opt-in maximum is not the kernel's maximum, and the safety margin that failed a passing gate\n428:## 19. The variance is BETWEEN checkpoint loads, not within them — 0.6 % vs 5.7 %\n471:## 20. A gate that does not compile is a gate that passes by never running (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n519:## 21. dprof reads a saving 15–20 % low, so it attributes but does not ratchet (ladder 1.5)\n542:## 22. `tau` reproduced to four decimals; `tok/s` on the same protocol did not — and the promotion gate keys on the second one (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
