{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEEtU16Yur8ugvUaeopF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011YCxjXLitK3MG1ckAYfuvY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; python3 - <<'PY'\np='DECODE_LADDER.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"      the reason it gets its own item and not\n      a footnote. [`measurement-and-traps.md` §22.2]\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1\nnew = \"\"\"      the reason it gets its own item and not\n      a footnote. [`measurement-and-traps.md` §22.2]\n\n      **ANSWERED 2026-08-20 by 3.1, and the reading in this entry was the right one: it is the\n      measurement.** `WARM decode` is a 7-step average taken immediately after load — i.e. inside\n      the ~2 s governor ramp — so it times the governor, not the engine. Six loads today, same\n      binary, same gate prompt, same protocol, differing only in whether the rails were pinned:\n\n      | machine state | base AR (`WARM decode`) |\n      |---|---|\n      | governed | **88.0 / 88.0 / 88.7 / 88.4 ms/tok** (11.36 / 11.36 / 11.27 / 11.31 tok/s) |\n      | pinned | **72.7 / 72.9 ms/tok** (13.75 / 13.72 tok/s) |\n\n      That is **+21.0 to +21.7 %**, it reproduces to a tenth of a millisecond in both states, and it\n      is the whole of the 72.5 -> 87.7/88.2 \"fall\". The earlier numbers were taken on a pinned box\n      and the later ones were not; HARDWARE.md predicted exactly this at **+20.7 %** in 2026-08-07\n      and named the mechanism (\"that window is measured immediately after load, before the governor\n      has ramped\"), and nobody connected the two because no run recorded its clock state. **There is\n      no 17.4 % engine regression.** Speculative throughput being flat across the same runs, which\n      this entry flagged as the reason to doubt the regression, is exactly right: the suite runs\n      after the ramp, so it never saw it.\n\n      **Left unchecked deliberately.** 3.1 supplies the mechanism and the six-load table; what 2.5\n      still owns is the consequence it names — every \"N.NNx vs base AR\" ratio in this repo has a\n      denominator that depends on a clock state nobody recorded, and those ratios need re-stating\n      against the pinned 72.8 ms/tok now that `run_model.sh` pins by default. That is a sweep through\n      the archive, not a measurement, and it should be its own iteration.\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new)); print(\"2.5 annotated\")\nPY\ngrep -c '' DECODE_LADDER.md","description":"Annotate item 2.5 with 3.1's finding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2127,"cache_read_input_tokens":133672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2127},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd851466-8fe9-421b-9d36-f2763d695418","uuid":"7e6b56f1-990d-49e1-b78b-da58477a4d0b","timestamp":"2026-08-20T15:31:02.580Z","request_id":"req_011CeEEtSuMzuM2uDVC1Azar"}
