{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEF5NYEuTAkEFRgvYdbn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012s4PuZisN15Kg5BxvFWVef","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_3p1.txt <<'MSG'\n3.1: the clock lever was already applied -- pinning buys the 2 s ramp, not the ceiling\n\nDECODE_LADDER 3.1 read \"jetson_clocks -- GPU 1386 -> 1575 MHz, EMC 2750 -> 4266, measured\nin-repo at +3.0-6.4 %\". Both halves are wrong about this workload, and one sampler settled it.\n\nWHAT THE RAILS ACTUALLY DO. No run in this repo had ever sampled a clock while a decode was in\nflight. Every 2 s, across three governed arms: 97.7 % of compute-window samples sit at 1386 MHz\nand 4266 MHz -- the pinned frequencies. The 315 MHz / 2750 MHz state everyone read as \"the run\"\nis the ~90 s checkpoint load, when the GPU is idle and the CPU is reading 100 GiB. Both rails\nramp to their ceiling within ~2 s of the GPU going busy, with no pin at all.\n\nSO THE MEASURED GAIN IS THE RAMP: +1.99 +/- 0.15 % on the frozen suite (8/8 legs positive)\nagainst the closest-in-time governed arm, +2.96 % against a time-interpolated one, drift control\n+2.03 +/- 0.99 %. Below the 3.5 % run-to-run spread. NOT counted as a ladder win. tau is 3.8438\nin all six arms of both runs, to four decimals -- the negative control this item needed, since\nclocks cannot change which token wins an argmax.\n\nMAXN's 1575 MHz is worth +1.68 +/- 5.83 % -- nothing, which is the right answer for a\nbandwidth-bound engine asked about its core clock. (jetson_clocks cannot reach 1575 anyway: it\nraises a rail to its governor's ceiling and nvpmodel 1 caps GPU MAX_FREQ at 1386000000.) The\ndeployment pins at the current power mode and never touches nvpmodel.\n\nADOPTED ANYWAY, FOR THE MEASUREMENT. base AR (`WARM decode`) is a 7-step average taken\nimmediately after load -- inside the ramp -- so it times the governor: 88.0 / 88.0 / 88.7 / 88.4\nms/tok governed against 72.7 / 72.9 pinned, six loads, reproducing to a tenth of a millisecond in\nboth states. That 21 % artefact IS ladder item 2.5's unexplained \"17.4 % base-AR regression\", in\nfull. There is no engine regression; spec throughput never moved because the suite runs after the\nramp. HARDWARE.md predicted this at +20.7 % on 2026-08-07 and nobody connected it, because no run\nrecorded its clock state. scripts/pin_clocks.sh now does, from run_model.sh and run_server.sh,\nwith a <log>.clocks sidecar per run.\n\nTHE FIRST ATTEMPT VOIDED ITSELF, AND THAT IS THE MORE USEFUL HALF. clocks_ab_run.sh pre-registered\n\"if A' does not come back to A the whole comparison is void\". A' came back +8.19 % -- larger than\nthe +5.70 % pinning was supposed to be worth. Cause: the agent supervising the arms kept working\nduring them, and a ~GB node process of its own exited inside arm C's one backwards leg (22.97 ->\n14.37 tok/s with the core clock flat at 1575 and power dropping 34 W -> 19.5 W). Re-run on a quiet\nbox: drift control 8.19 % -> 1.78 %, and the engine reproduces tau on all 9 prompts instead of 8.\nA measurement arm is single-tenant and the agent is a tenant. Only the repeat of an already-run arm\ncaught it -- tau, LOSSLESS and the first-token gate all passed in all four contaminated arms.\n\nEvidence: evidence/decode_loop/clocks_3p1_ab.txt (the void run, kept), clocks_emc_report.txt,\nclocks_emc_{A2,B2,A2p}.{log,samples}.\nWiki: negative-results.md §4e, measurement-and-traps.md §23 + §24, hardware-sm110a.md §5,\nHARDWARE.md, README state table. New stage clocks_emc_probe.sh registered in detach_audit.sh.\nMSG\necho \"written\"; ls -la evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_3p1.txt","description":"Write the prepared commit message"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1557,"cache_read_input_tokens":145448,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1557},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd851466-8fe9-421b-9d36-f2763d695418","uuid":"34282207-1215-42d9-b2af-37ad7ab6125f","timestamp":"2026-08-20T15:33:36.309Z","request_id":"req_011CeEF5MVjjoA2f7eq32kde"}
